rds; a hypothetical plateau is not an added premise of the full-support theorem. Time 1 is outside the support domain; this route does not assume a contact point or derivative there. Includes c=0 and does not appeal to infinite support as an extra premise. The minimizer premise here belongs to the ordinary manuscript model; formal-interface hypotheses remain on the separate Lean target. This classification does not prove a transport between formal models.","citation_ids":["support_terminal_source","support_terminal_lean_source","support_closure_source"],"evidence_ids":["support_source_bindings_20261024","support_graph_semantic_review_pending"],"id":"support.no_terminal_gap","kind":"claim","label":"A minimizer has no terminal plateau or empty support","locator":"variation.tex:130–213 and 215–221; lem:no-terminal-plateau","source_id":"support_tex_variation","statement":"For every admissible minimizer gamma, there do not exist 0<=a<1 and finite c>=0 with gamma=c on (a,1). Indeed the terminal defect yields q(t)-t<0 near 1 and hence G(s)<0 for s sufficiently close to 1, contradicting G>=0. In particular support cannot be empty, since that would force gamma=0.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.no_terminal_gap","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.no_terminal_gap","id":"field:17055e519e60be0f708b7a6d4db8289e3131d10a49456b7a0ffc978a886ce21c","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.no_terminal_gap","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/scalar.paper_minimizer"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/